 (filename path)←x IdentifyObject name;buff;space;token;isAbsolute;rc;msg
⍝ Takes an APL name or a filename and returns the name of the file, relative to the root of the
⍝ Git project, together with the path of that project.\\
⍝ `name` is interpreted like this:
⍝ * When it carries a path separator it is a filename:
⍝   * An absolute path just has to point into a Git-managed folder: Git itself establishes the
⍝     root of it. Neither does a project have to be open, nor does it have to be a project at
⍝     all, and `x` is not even looked at.
⍝   * Anything else is relative to the root of the project. A leading "./" is permitted; it
⍝     just emphasises that the path starts at the root, and is removed.
⍝ * Without any path separator it might still be a filename, so three things are tried in
⍝   this order: a well-formed APL name that actually exists, a file in the root of the
⍝   project, and finally a file of that name in the source folder of the project. When
⍝   that last one finds more than one match the user is asked which one she means.\\
⍝ Note that every path returned by this package - by `Status`, `Log`, `Diff` etc. - is relative
⍝ to the root of the project as well, so whatever they report can be fed back in as `name`.\\
⍝ For what `x` can actually be see `EstablishProject`.
 token←name
 isAbsolute←(':'∊name)∨(⊃name,' ')∊'/\'
 :If ~isAbsolute                       ⍝ Only then do we need to establish the project at all
     (space path)←EstablishProject x
     'Not a Cider/acre project'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨0=≢path
 :EndIf
 :If ∨/'/\:'∊name
     filename←F.EnforceSlash name
     :If isAbsolute
         (rc msg buff)←(⊃⎕NPARTS filename)U.RunGitCommand'rev-parse --show-toplevel'
         ('Not a Git-managed folder: ',name)U.Assert 0=rc
         path←U.NormalizeFolder∊buff
         space←GetProjectFromPath path  ⍝ Empty unless it happens to be an opened project
         filename←(1+≢path)↓filename
     :Else
         filename←{'./'≡2↑⍵:2↓⍵ ⋄ ⍵}filename
     :EndIf
 :Else
     filename←''
     :If ~(⊃name)∊'#⎕'
     :AndIf 0<≢space                   ⍝ Without a project space it cannot be qualified, so it is no APL name
         name←space,'.',name
     :EndIf
     :If (⊃name)∊'#⎕'                  ⍝ Only a qualified name can possibly be an APL object
     :AndIf 0<⎕NC name                 ⍝ Is it REALLY one? "Foo.aplf" is a well-formed name, too!
         filename←GetFileName name
         ('Could not establish the filename that hosts ',name)Assert 0<≢filename
         filename←(1+≢path)↓filename
     :EndIf
     :If 0=≢filename
     :AndIf F.IsFile path,'/',token     ⍝ A file in the root of the project?
         filename←token
     :EndIf
     :If 0=≢filename
         filename←path U.FindFileInSourceFolder token
         ('Neither an APL object nor a file: ',token)Assert 0<≢filename
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 filename←F.EnforceSlash filename   ⍝ One canonical form, no matter which branch established it
⍝Done
